<title>USA: Fed refrains from open market operations.</title>
<headline>Fed refrains from open market operations.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve refrained from open market operations on Friday, as expected, dealers said.</p>
<p>Analysts had said the banking system's need for reserves had been met by the Fed's temporary addition of reserves on Thursday through seven-day fixed system repurchase agreements.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at 5-7/16 percent, below the Fed's 5-1/2 percent target for the rate, at mid-morning.</p>
<p>-- ((E. Freilich, North American Treasury Desk 212-859-1679((</p>
</text>
